diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 9fb62ad..fc20bfd 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- C++ member calls resolve through the receiver's type: a local (`Engine e;`), a parameter (`Pump* p`, `const Pump& p`), a member of a typed struct (`b.engine.start()`, a bare member name or `this->` inside a method of its class), `auto e = Engine();`, `auto p = std::make_unique<Pump>();` (also `make_shared`, `new`, casts, smart pointers, `using` aliases, range-for variables and a function's return type) reach the right class's method with certainty, so `callers` of `Engine.start` no longer marks them as guesses among every class with a `start`. A receiver whose type cannot be told, or a class that does not define the method itself (it inherits it), stays a guess by name. Functions and methods returning a pointer or reference and `using` aliases are indexed. Schema 25; C++ files re-parse once.
 - `callers` of a C function-pointer member lists the lines storing a function in it (`.irq_mask = foo_mask,`) as their own group after the call sites, `stores a function in it (not calls): N`, no longer among the references that are not calls, and they no longer make the answer read as incomplete. `callers` of a function counts the documentation lines naming it after the verdict (`plus N in docs (not code, not listed)`) and never lists them.
 - The SubagentStart brief no longer carries the swarm board protocol line by default: in A/B runs it gave parallel subagents nothing and cost more. `[hooks] swarm_board = true` in `config.toml` brings it back. The parent packet and parent read lines stay.
 
